==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[to]] [[take]] [[the]] [[cake]]|takes the cake|taking the cake|took the cake|taken the cake}}
# {{context|idiomatic|US|lang=en}} To be especially [[good]] or [[outstanding]].  
#: ''Thanks!  You guys '''take the cake'''.''
#: ''Once the party was over, everyone agreed that Elizabeth and her Harriet Tubman getup had '''taken the cake'''.''
# {{context|idiomatic|US|lang=en}} To be particularly [[bad]], [[objectionable]], or [[egregious]].
#: ''I've seen bad grammar, but this '''takes the cake'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to be good or outstanding)}} [[steal the show]]
* {{sense|to be particularly bad or egregious}} [[take the biscuit]]  (''British'')

